# Server
PORT=3000

# Sentiment provider selection: inference | placeholder
# - inference (default): calls an OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint,
#   configured below. Works with local Ollama, Groq, or any other OpenAI-
#   compatible API -- swap providers by changing INFERENCE_BASE_URL/
#   INFERENCE_MODEL alone, no code changes needed. (Configurable this way at
#   Echory's explicit request, so they can point this backend at an external
#   model if the local one has problems on their side.)
# - placeholder: rule-based, no LLM, no external dependency at all. Not the
#   default -- ticket 0016 made the real local model the default so what you
#   run matches what actually gets evaluated -- but still available as a
#   manual override (set LLM_PROVIDER=placeholder) if you want to see the
#   API/UI working without installing Ollama or holding an API key.
LLM_PROVIDER=inference

# Used when LLM_PROVIDER=inference. Default below is the final choice from
# tickets 0006 (local benchmark) + 0015 (cloud comparison): phi4-mini (3.8B,
# local via Ollama). Full numbers and reasoning in docs/benchmark-results.md
# and both tickets' logs -- summary:
#
#   Model              | Sentiment acc | Risk acc | Avg latency | % calls > 500ms
#   phi4-mini (chosen) |      82%       |   75%    |   408ms     |       0%
#   groq/qwen3.8-27b   |      93%       |   71%    |   378ms     |      14%
#
# qwen3.8-27b beats phi4-mini on accuracy AND average latency, holdout-
# confirmed (not overfitting, unlike an earlier candidate). Declined anyway:
# its 14% chance of exceeding 500ms comes from Groq-side queue/network
# variance, not something a prompt or code change can fix (measured directly),
# and the challenge scores latency as a pass/fail cliff ("consistently
# exceeding 500ms counts as a failure"), not a smooth penalty -- risking that
# 25%-weighted dimension for a partial gain in the 30%-weighted accuracy
# dimension (where phi4-mini already scores respectably) was judged not worth
# it. Measured from Felix's own network to Groq; an evaluator's network has no
# guarantee of being comparable. Genuinely close call, not a clear-cut one --
# see docs/benchmark-results.md if this needs to be revisited.
#
# granite4.1:3b is the safer local alternative (70% accuracy, larger latency
# margin than phi4-mini's already-safe 0%). Switch via INFERENCE_MODEL alone:
#   INFERENCE_MODEL=granite4.1:3b
#
# All three are non-reasoning models, so the default OpenAI-compatible path
# below works cleanly for any of them -- INFERENCE_DISABLE_THINKING is not
# needed unless a future model choice turns out to require it (ticket 0005/0007).
#
# This setup is Docker-only (ticket 0016) -- there is no supported native
# `npm start` path anymore, per Pascal's explicit preference for Docker. The
# backend always runs in a container; Ollama currently runs natively on the
# host (not yet containerized -- see ticket 0017, blocked pending Pascal's
# input on whether GPU passthrough into a container is workable on Echory's
# side, since that risk is real: no GPU passthrough at all on Docker Desktop
# for Mac, and it needs the NVIDIA Container Toolkit configured on Windows/
# Linux -- without it, phi4-mini would fall back to slow CPU inference and
# could blow the 500ms latency line). Because of that, `host.docker.internal`
# (not `localhost`) is required below -- inside the container, `localhost`
# means the container itself, not the machine running Ollama. Docker Desktop
# resolves `host.docker.internal` to the host automatically on Windows/Mac.
INFERENCE_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
INFERENCE_MODEL=phi4-mini
INFERENCE_API_KEY=

# ---- If the local Ollama setup has trouble on Echory's side ----
# Per Pascal's explicit request, switching to a cloud provider needs zero
# code changes -- just replace the three lines above with these three
# (verified working, ticket 0015; not the plan's original
# llama-3.3-70b-versatile, which no longer exists in Groq's catalog --
# verified via their /models endpoint, not assumed):
#   INFERENCE_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   INFERENCE_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.8-27b
#   INFERENCE_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key

# Opt-in escape hatch (ticket 0007), OFF by default. Only relevant if
# INFERENCE_MODEL above is switched to a local *reasoning* model -- Ollama's
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint above cannot suppress "thinking" mode
# (think:false is silently ignored there), only Ollama's native /api/chat
# respects it (verified in ticket 0005). When set to true, the same
# InferenceProvider routes to native /api/chat with think:false instead of
# the default OpenAI-compatible call, derived from INFERENCE_BASE_URL by
# dropping the trailing /v1 -- no second base-URL var needed. Never set this
# for a cloud provider (Groq, etc.) -- it only makes sense for local Ollama.
# Not needed for phi4-mini/granite4.1:3b (both non-reasoning); verified
# working against a real local reasoning model (qwen3:8b) during this
# ticket's manual check even though the current model choice never exercises
# it in production.
INFERENCE_DISABLE_THINKING=false

# Only used by scripts/llm-benchmark.ts (ticket 0006's local model quality
# benchmark) -- NOT required to run the actual backend. An external judge
# (rather than another local model) avoids competing with the models under
# test for the same GPU. DeepSeek's API is OpenAI-compatible.
JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
JUDGE_MODEL=deepseek-reasoner
JUDGE_API_KEY=your-deepseek-api-key
